I can think of at least three ways to do this:

1) By reading it.  You'll find out in a hurry what it does :).
2) By dropping it in a shop. The shopkeeper will offer you a price for
it. Or, if you pick up a scroll in a shop, the shopkeeper will offer to
sell it to you for a price.  This gives you a clue as to the type of
scroll it could be.  For example,  a particular scroll is always the
cheapest one in the game.   If the shopkeeper offers to sell you a
scroll for, say , 600 gold, you know it's not *that* particular scroll.
  Instead, you know it's one of the four or so different types of
scroll that can be bought for 600.

You can figure out what the price ranges are for different kind of
scrolls by buying or selling known scrolls. ... or by going to
steelypips and reading the scroll spoiler.

3) By seeing what a monster does with it.  For example,  if a monster
reads a scroll of READ ME and disappears, you know it's a scroll of
teleportation.  

